                  "code": "PARSECERTIFICATE",
                  "convergenceTargetId": "1763970618907",
                  "id": "1763109974729",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1763109974731_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are a careful information extraction assistant. Extract the requested fields from the proof of good health document. Return only valid *formatted* JSON that conforms exactly to the schema below. Do not include any extra explanation, commentary, or markdown â€” just the *formatted* JSON.\nYou must follow the steps in order and obey all negative constraints.\n\nYou must never reuse inferred or classified information to populate extracted fields.\n\n***Constraints***\n\n\t-Only analyze text strictly between the markers:\n\t<--BEGIN PEC TEXT--> ... <--END PEC TEXT-->\n\t-Extract fields according to the schema.\n\t-Remove page numbers, line numbers, OCR hyphenation, and normalize whitespace.\n\t-Use ISO 8601 (YYYY-MM-DD) for all dates. If the day is missing and month/year are known, set the date to null rather than guessing.\n\t-If a field is not found or is ambiguous, set it to the JSON null literal (not an empty string).\n\t-If multiple plausible values exist (e.g., more than one policy number), include an array in the field and populate primary where possible.\n\t-Return only the final JSON object. No extra text.\n\n***DOCUMENT CLASSIFICATION***\t\n         -DocumentType: Classify the document as PROOF_OF_EXTERNAL_COVERAGE based on the below criteria and return only the confidence score on a scale from 0 to 1, where 0 means no confidence and 1 means full confidence.\n\t      STEP1: Do NOT classify as PROOF_OF_EXTERNAL_COVERAGE classification and confidence MUST be 0 if the document is any one of the following:\n\t\t\t- A medical report or health questionnaire\n\t\t\t- Evidence of insurability / proof of good health\n\t\t\t- A claim, bill, or premium receipt without coverage confirmation\n\t\t\t- An internal enrollment or benefits election form\n                        - An insurance approval letter\n\t\t\t-if the document contains any of the following indicators:\n\t\t\t\t- â€œEvidence of Insurabilityâ€?\n\t\t\t\t- â€œHealth Applicationâ€?\n\t\t\t\t- â€œMedical Underwritingâ€?\n\t\t\t\t- â€œCoverage applied forâ€?\n\t\t\t\t- â€œCoverage requestedâ€?\n\t\t\t\t- â€œSubject to approvalâ€?\n\t\t\t\t- â€œWill become effective if approvedâ€?\n\t\t\t\t- â€œProof of good healthâ€?\n\t\t\t\t- â€œHealth Statementâ€?\n\t\t\t\t- â€œApplication for insuranceâ€?\t\n                   - STOP classification immediately\n                  - Do NOT evaluate any positive criteria\n                  - Do NOT consider insurer names, policy numbers, coverage tables, dates, or benefits\n              STEP2 â€” POSITIVE QUALIFICATION:\n                   -Only if Step 1 does NOT trigger, evaluate criteria 1â€“5 for PROOF_OF_EXTERNAL_COVERAGE.\n                   -A document qualifies as PROOF_OF_EXTERNAL_COVERAGE ONLY IF it clearly shows:\n\t\t1. Coverage provided by an external insurer or employer\n\t\t2. Type of coverage (e.g., medical, life, health, disability)\n\t\t3. Evidence that coverage is active or valid (dates or explicit status)\n\t\t4. A clear link to the individual (name, policy number or relationship)\n\t\t5.Coverage state rule (mandatory):\n\t\t\tThe document qualifies as PROOF_OF_EXTERNAL_COVERAGE ONLY IF it explicitly confirms coverage is active, in force, or valid as of a stated date.\n\t\t\t**If the document does NOT contain an explicit affirmative statement that coverage is active, in force, or enrolled, classification confidence MUST be 0**\n\t\t\tDocuments that discuss coverage that is:\n\t\t\t- applied for\n\t\t\t- requested\n\t\t\t- subject to underwriting\n\t\t\t- pending approval\n\t\t\t- requiring evidence of insurability\n\t\t\t- conditional or future-dated upon approval\n\t\t\tMUST NOT be classified as PROOF_OF_EXTERNAL_COVERAGE and classification confidence MUST be 0.\n\t\t\n\t\t*IMPORTANT*\t\t\n\t\t-Produce ONLY an internal numeric confidence value and populate the *DocumentType*\n\t\t-DO NOT extract or populate any other fields in this step\n\t\t-DO NOT reuse results of this step later\n\t\t\n***Extraction rules***\n\t-Name: Capture the name of the person for whom the document has been provided as proof.\n\t-Provider: identify and return only the insurance provider name.Ignore all other content.If multiple insurance entities are listed, return the primary insurance provider or issuing company referenced in the document. \n\t-PolicyNumber: capture the coverage â€œPolicy Numberâ€? or â€œGroup Policy Numberâ€? ONLY if explicitly labeled as such.\n\t\t-Do NOT use any other identifier as a Policy Number.\n\t\t-If no Policy Number or Group Policy Number is explicitly present, return an empty array.\n\t-coverageType: Capture the name of the coverage for which this document has been provided as proof. Capture only if the name of the coverage plan has been mentioned explicitly. Do not infer.\n\t\t- Do NOT extract this field from:\n\t\t  - document titles or document names\n\t\t  - section headers\n\t\t  - page headers or footers\n\t\t  - generic phrases such as â€œHealth Insurance Coverageâ€?\n\n\t\t-Do NOT use generic insurance categories (health, medical, life, disability).\n\n\t\t-If no explicit plan or product name is present under a coverage field, set coverageType to null.\n\t\t\n\t\t-If multiple explicit coverage descriptors are present:\n\t\t\t- Use â€œPlan Typeâ€? values ONLY if coverage plan name or coverage type is not present.\n\t\n\t-CoverageDate: Capture the start date of the coverage.\n \n***Normalization***\n\n\t-Trim strings; collapse spaces.\n\t-Title-case names; uppercase state codes; normalize US ZIP to 5 or 9 digits (ZIP+4 allowed with dash).\n\t-Validate all dates; if invalid or partial, set to null.\n\n***Ambiguity resolution***\n\n\t-Prefer entities closest to explicit labels.\n\n***Empty or invalid input***\n\n\t-If no usable text is found, return the JSON with all fields null and empty arrays and set DocumentParseSuccessful to false. If even one field could be extracted then DocumentParseSuccessful should be true.\n\nInput\n\t<--BEGIN PEC TEXT-->\n\t{{$context.$nodes.PENDINGCERTIFICATIONSLOOP.FETCHCERTIFICATIONDOCUMENT.$output.text}}\n\t<--END PEC TEXT-->\n\nOutput JSON schema (use null for missing values)\n{\n  \"Provider\": null,\n  \"PolicyNumbers\": [],\n  \"Name\": null,\n  \"coverageType\": null,\n  \"DocumentType\": null,\n  \"CoverageDate\": null,\n  \"DocumentParseSuccessful\":false\n}\n\nFallbacks & heuristics\n\n\tIf insurance provider is not explicitly stated but an issuer is referenced repeatedly in headers/footers, use that issuer as insurance_provider with confidence based on frequency."
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"Provider\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"PolicyNumbers\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {}\n            }\n        },\n        \"Name\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"CoverageType\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"DocumentType\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n\t\"CoverageDate\": {\n\t\t\"type\":\"string\"\n\t},\n        \"DocumentParseSuccessful\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "document_parse_successful"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "true": "1763365114545",
                    "false": "1764338975016"
                  },
                  "code": "DOCUMENTPARSESUCCESSFUL",
                  "convergenceTargetId": "end_1762863428229",
                  "id": "1763975433480",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1763975433482_1",
                      "name": "condition",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "{{$context.$nodes.PENDINGCERTIFICATIONSLOOP.PARSECERTIFICATE.$output.DocumentParseSuccessful == true}}"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "CONDITION"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "modelConfiguration": {
                      "modelProperties": {},
                      "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
                      "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM",
                      "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
                      "modelName": "GPT-5 mini"
                    },
                    "name": "matchDocument"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1763465070677"
                  },
                  "code": "MATCHDOCUMENT",
                  "convergenceTargetId": "1763975813567",
                  "id": "1763365114545",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1763365114550_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "SYSTEM:\n\nYou are a document matching engine. Your job is to compare an extracted document JSON (DOCUMENT_JSON) to a set of target variables (TARGET) and return a single JSON result that shows per-attribute scores, weighted contributions, overall score, and a final match decision.\n\nIMPORTANT RULES:\n\n\t-OUTPUT ONLY JSON (no explanations, no extra text).\n\n\t-Round numeric scores to two decimals.\n\n\t-Follow normalization and matching rules below exactly.\n\nUSER:\n\n\tYou will receive two inputs:\n\n\tDOCUMENT_JSON: {{$context.$nodes.PENDINGCERTIFICATIONSLOOP.PARSECERTIFICATE.$output}}\n\n\tTARGET variables:\n\n\t{\n\t  \"Name\": {{$context.$variables.displayName}},  \n\t  \"CoverageDate\": {{$context.$system.$currentDate }}\n\t}\n\nNORMALIZATION (apply before comparing):\n\n\t-Lowercase all text and trim whitespace.\n\n\t-Collapse multiple spaces to one.\n\n\t-Remove punctuation from names and providers (commas, periods, parentheses, extra slashes).\n\n\t-Dates: Normalize to YYYY-MM-DD. If parsing fails, treat as a mismatch and return a 0.00 score for CoverageDate.\n\n\tMATCH TYPES:\n\n\t-exact:\n\n\t\t-CoverageDate in DOCUMENT_JSON should be less than or equal to CoverageDate in TARGET.\n\n\t\t-Exact match scoring:\n\n\t\t\t-Score = 1.00 if the dates are valid (i.e., not null or in an invalid format) and CoverageDate in DOCUMENT_JSON is less than or equal to (CoverageDate +90 days) in TARGET.\n\n\t\t\t-Score = 0.00 if the dates are missing, or cannot be parsed or CoverageDate in DOCUMENT_JSON is greater than CoverageDate in TARGET\n                       -Date parsing: Convert the string to a valid date object and compare.\n\n\t-fuzzy:\n\n\t\t-Name: Compute similarity âˆˆ [0.00, 1.00]. Use token overlap (Dice coefficient) and string metric such as Jaro-Winkler.\n\n\t-existence:\n\n\t\t-Provider: Return true if it exists (not null).\n\n\t\t-PolicyNumber: Return true if it exists (not null).\n\n\t\t-CoverageType: Return true if it exists (not null).\n\nSIMILARITY GUIDANCE (for implementer or LLM):\n\n\t-For names, allow for missing middle names or initials and treat token order as tolerant.\n\n\t-For string comparison, use token overlap (Dice coefficient) and Jaro-Winkler distance.\n\nWEIGHTING:\n\n\t-DocumentType: weight = 0.30\n\n\t-Name: weight = 0.30\n\n\t-Provider: weight = 0.10\n\n\t-PolicyNumber: weight = 0.10\n\n\t-CoverageType: weight = 0.10\n\n\t-CoverageDate: weight = 0.10\n\nSCORING RULES:\n\n\t-exact match attributes:\n\n\t\t-score = 1.00 if the attribute is not null and valid, else score = 0.00.\n\n\t-existence attributes:\n\n\t\t-score = 1.00 if the attribute exists (not null or empty), else score = 0.00.\n\n\t-fuzzy attributes:\n\n\t\t-score = computed similarity âˆˆ [0.00, 1.00].\n\n\t-DocumentType: Fetch the score from DOCUMENT_JSON directly (using the confidence value).\n\n\t-weighted_score = score * weight.\n\n\t-overall_score = sum of all weighted scores (DocumentType, Name, Provider, PolicyNumber, CoverageType, CoverageDate).\n\n\t-decision threshold: 0.80 â†’ overall_score >= 0.80 => \"MATCH\", else \"NO_MATCH\".\n\nOUTPUT JSON SCHEMA (RETURN ONLY THIS JSON):\n{\n    \"DocumentType\": {\n      \"doc_value\": string|null,\n      \"target_value\": null,\n      \"match_type\": \"fuzzy\",\n      \"score\": 0.00-1.00,\n      \"weight\": 0.30,\n      \"weighted_score\": 0.00-0.30\n    },\n    \"Name\": {\n      \"doc_value\": string|null,\n      \"target_value\": string,\n      \"match_type\": \"fuzzy\",\n      \"score\": 0.00-1.00,\n      \"weight\": 0.30,\n      \"weighted_score\": 0.00-0.30\n    },\n    \"Provider\": {\n      \"doc_value\": string|null,\n      \"target_value\": null,\n      \"match_type\": \"exist\",\n      \"score\": 0.00-1.00,\n      \"weight\": 0.10,\n      \"weighted_score\": 0.00-0.10\n    },\n    \"PolicyNumber\": {\n      \"doc_value\": string|array|null,\n      \"target_value\": null,\n      \"match_type\": \"exist\",\n      \"score\": 0.00-1.00,\n      \"weight\": 0.10,\n      \"weighted_score\": 0.00-0.10\n    },\n    \"CoverageType\": {\n      \"doc_value\": string|null,\n      \"target_value\": null,\n      \"match_type\": \"exist\",\n      \"score\": 0.00-1.00,\n      \"weight\": 0.10,\n      \"weighted_score\": 0.00-0.10\n    },\n    \"CoverageDate\": {\n      \"doc_value\": string|null,\n      \"target_value\": string|null,\n      \"match_type\": \"exact\",\n      \"score\": 0.00-1.00,\n      \"weight\": 0.10,\n      \"weighted_score\": 0.00-0.10\n    },\n    \"overall_score\": 0.00-1.00,\n    \"match_decision\": \"MATCH\"|\"NO_MATCH\",\n    \"decision_threshold\": 0.80\n}\n\nADDITIONAL OUTPUT RULES:\n\n\t-Round all numeric scores to two decimals.\n\n\t-Include actual CoverageDate values (both from DOCUMENT_JSON and TARGET) in the output JSON.\n        \n        -Return the JSON attributes in the same order as mentioned in OUTPUT JSON SCHEMA\n\nEXAMPLE (illustrative):\n\nDOCUMENT_JSON:\n\n{\n  \"Provider\": \"The Hartford\",\n  \"PolicyNumbers\": [\"677347\", \"703586\"],\n  \"Name\": \"Lee Buddy\",\n  \"CoverageType\": [\"Insurance\"],\n  \"DocumentType\": {\n    \"type\": \"PROOF_OF_EXTERNAL_COVERAGE\",\n    \"confidence\": 0.95\n  },\n  \"CoverageDate\": \"2025-01-01\"\n}\n\n\nTARGET:\n\n{\n  \"Provider\": true,\n  \"PolicyNumber\": true,\n  \"Name\": \"Lee Buddy\",\n  \"CoverageType\": true,\n  \"DocumentType\": \"PROOF_OF_EXTERNAL_COVERAGE\",\n  \"CoverageDate\": \"2025-02-01\"\n}\n\n\nEXPECTED OUTPUT:\n\n{\n    \"DocumentType\": { \n      \"doc_value\": \"PROOF_OF_EXTERNAL_COVERAGE\", \n      \"target_value\":null, \n      \"match_type\": \"fuzzy\", \n      \"score\": 1.00, \n      \"weight\": 0.30, \n      \"weighted_score\": 0.30\n    },\n    \"Name\": { \n      \"doc_value\": \"Lee Buddy\", \n      \"target_value\": \"Lee Buddy\", \n      \"match_type\": \"fuzzy\", \n      \"score\": 1.00, \n      \"weight\": 0.30, \n      \"weighted_score\": 0.30\n    },\n    \"Provider\": { \n      \"doc_value\": \"The Hartford\", \n      \"target_value\": null, \n      \"match_type\": \"exist\", \n      \"score\": 1.00, \n      \"weight\": 0.10, \n      \"weighted_score\": 0.10\n    },\n    \"PolicyNumber\": { \n      \"doc_value\": [\"677347\", \"703586\"], \n      \"target_value\": null, \n      \"match_type\": \"exist\", \n      \"score\": 1.00, \n      \"weight\": 0.10, \n      \"weighted_score\": 0.10\n    },\n    \"CoverageType\": { \n      \"doc_value\": [\"Insurance\"], \n      \"target_value\": null, \n      \"match_type\": \"exist\", \n      \"score\": 1.00, \n      \"weight\": 0.10, \n      \"weighted_score\": 0.10\n    },\n    \"CoverageDate\": { \n      \"doc_value\": \"2025-01-01\", \n      \"target_value\": \"2025-02-01\", \n      \"match_type\": \"exact\", \n      \"score\": 0.95, \n      \"weight\": 0.10, \n      \"weighted_score\": 0.095\n    },\n    \"overall_score\": 0.895,\n    \"match_decision\": \"MATCH\",\n    \"decision_threshold\": 0.80\n}"
